<title>FRANCE: Union wins court ruling on Renault.</title>
<headline>Union wins court ruling on Renault.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French carmaker Renault SA will present a new plan for 272 job cuts at its Boulogne-Billancourt headquarters after a court ruled its procedure violated the law.</p>
<p>&quot;We need to hold a new meeting with staff representatives and provide better documentation (on the plan),&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The Communist-led CGT union brought the action against Renault for the 1996 and 1997 job plans. The court in Nanterre outside Paris ruled against Renault on the 1997 plan and fined the company 150,000 francs but ruled in its favour on the 1996 plan.</p>
<p>Renault has proposed 2,764 job cuts in France this year out of a total staff of around 141,000.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
